Dome tree by TGlad (Tom Lowe): a dome that sprouts a ring of smaller
domes, each of which sprouts its own ring, and so on, built from circle
inversions (DomeTree.frag in github.com/TGlad/FragmentariumExamples).

Calculated by mb3d-rs itself (the code above is only a placeholder; the
original Mandelbulb3D shows nothing with this formula).

Levels: how deep the tree goes (up to 100).
Children: the domes in each ring (4 .. 10).
Bend angle: in radians, how far the domes bulge (low: flat discs, high:
round domes); 0.3 .. 1.3 work best, above that the surface turns grainy.
Colour scale: each branch gets its own colour value (0..2, the orbit
trap: "2nd choice" in the Lighting); this scales it.
Start curved: 1 starts with the first dome bent into a ball, 0 starts
with a flat floor that grows the first ring.

Use a small Raystep (0.2; 0.05 with 9 or 10 children) and 1 iteration.
